{"t":"2026-10-22T11:26:49.019Z","event":"finish","launch":"0099-cm-cs","n":2,"role":"cm-cs","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":40590,"cumulative":152642,"cost":0.3659,"turns":4,"minutes":0.68,"sessions":[],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I've delegated O-10 to the demo-builder. Nothing has been built yet.\n\n- **O-10 (LESSON-one-link-back-grows-the-core):** I ran `order delegate O-10 --by=cm-cs --to=demo-builder --budget=150000`. The order is now at the build stage, with build message M-11 waiting for the demo-builder. It's the only order in the queue, so splitting work across builders and `--after` chaining didn't come up.\n\nTwo things confused me:\n1. **Two budgets:** the order shows a budget of 6,000,000, and my delegation set 150,000. I don't know which one limits the build. My 150,000 went through as a separate budget message (M-10).\n2. **Who the orderer is:** the order lists chief-of-staff as orderer, but the accept text says \"orderer cm-cs (strand manager cm-cs-systems)\". It looks like a labelling mismatch and didn't stop the delegation.\n\nThe brief also says \"Build after web-bow-tie-reach (built)\", and the order isn't blocked, so there's nothing to wait for."}
