{"t":"2026-10-22T11:27:20.542Z","event":"finish","launch":"0098-cm-math","n":1,"role":"cm-math","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":42242,"cumulative":279979,"cost":0.4254,"turns":7,"minutes":1.22,"sessions":[],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I delegated all nine orders to `demo-builder`, each with a 150000 token budget. All nine are in its queue at the build stage.\n\n| Order | Lesson | Message ids | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| O-1 | push-the-frame-over | M-1, M-12 | delegated |\n| O-2 | ant-on-a-cube | M-2, M-13 | delegated |\n| O-3 | slice-a-corner-off | M-3, M-14 | delegated |\n| O-4 | friends-of-friends-overlap | M-4, M-15 | delegated |\n| O-5 | new-friend-loosens-the-circle | M-5, M-16 | delegated |\n| O-6 | not-every-circle-is-red | M-6, M-17 | delegated |\n| O-7 | regions-from-circle-points | M-7, M-18 | delegated |\n| O-8 | two-corners-off-the-board | M-8, M-19 | delegated |\n| O-9 | pick-two-or-pick-four | M-9, M-20 | delegated |\n\nWhat confused me:\n- **Only one builder to split across.** The brief says to split the orders across \"your builders\", but the roster has just one builder role, `demo-builder`. It runs 3 sessions at once and each session takes up to 2 items before stopping. So all nine had to go to the same role, and the split across sessions happens inside the role, not through how I delegate.\n- **The last three wait.** Three sessions taking two items each covers six orders. O-7, O-8 and O-9 will sit until a session frees up or a new one starts. That's my reading of the session settings, not something the tool confirmed.\n- **No orders depend on each other.** None has an `--after` link, so I couldn't group related items for one session. They'll be picked up in queue order.\n- **O-10 isn't mine.** O-10 (one-link-back-grows-the-core) is also at build, but it belongs to cm-cs, so I didn't touch it."}
