{"t":"2026-10-22T11:47:51.837Z","event":"finish","launch":"0107-demo-builder","n":3,"role":"demo-builder","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":179236,"cumulative":8121303,"cost":4.0734,"turns":79,"minutes":21.15,"sessions":["S-1"],"abandoned":[],"denials":2,"said":"I built both lessons and handed both in. Each passes the order's own check (the test1 check code will run), and the session closed at its cap of 2. QA, the walkthrough and fact-checking are later stages and haven't run yet.\n\n**1. O-10 one-link-back-grows-the-core (cs) → test1**\n- **What it is:** a 10-page bow-tie graph. Four buttons in the brief's order add I → F, add J → G, add both, or add none. The core is worked out live, filled in, and its links are drawn bold, with a \"core: N pages\" count. My own node check matches the brief: 4, 8, 6 and 10 pages.\n- **Gating:** the reveal unlocks after two steps, I → F (core 8, the question's own case) and J → G (core 6). Each button keeps a \"✓ N\" mark so going back to None doesn't erase what the reveal quotes. When the reveal opens, the graph switches back to the I → F case.\n- **Phone fit:** fits at 390×844 with nothing cut off at the top. My first reveal was 97 words, over the 90 limit, so I cut it to 86.\n- **Changes from the brief:**\n  - 4 claims, not the brief's 3: the general rule (\"one back link adds only the pages on the loop it closes\") is its own claim.\n  - Two link lines in the core cross once. With this layout the four-page loop can't be drawn without a crossing.\n  - The predict question is rewritten as a second-person scene, and the title and hook are mine.\n\n**2. O-4 friends-of-friends-overlap (math) → test1**\n- **What it is:** two pictures, one at a time. The village is a stretch of the 1,000-person ring with people coloured by how many steps away they are. \"No shared friends\" is a tree of 10, 90 and 810 people.\n- **Added to the brief:** from step 2, one friend is circled with its 10 links drawn: 7 land on you or your own friends, 3 are new. This puts the reason on the stage instead of only telling it in the reveal, and it adds a new claim.\n- **Changed from the brief:** its two readout lines became a small table with a village column and a \"no shared\" column. That keeps every number the reveal quotes on screen even after the learner switches back to the village.\n- **Phone fit:** fits at 390×844, nothing cut off at the top, reveal 80 words.\n\n**Things that confused me or might trip the next builder:**\n- **Claim types:** the kit only accepts derivation, simulation, source or convention as a claim's support. The briefs use \"definition\" and \"citation\", which the check rejects, so I used \"source\" and \"convention\" instead.\n- **Dev server side effects:** running the dev server in a worktree edits `tsconfig.json` and creates `AGENTS.md`. I reverted both in each worktree before handing in.\n- **Phone-fit tool timeout:** the reveal-fit tool timed out once because the page was still compiling. Loading the page with curl first fixed it.\n- **Missing endpoint:** the app logs a 404 for `/api/account/me` on every page. It isn't from these lessons, but QA fails a lesson on any console error, so it might trip the QA stage.\n- **Blocked commands:** the launcher blocks shell heredocs and `pkill`. I wrote files with the editor tools and stopped my servers as background tasks.\n- **Outside edit:** O-10's `meta.json` was changed on disk after I handed it in, presumably by code's stages. I didn't touch it."}
