{"t":"2026-10-22T11:48:50.174Z","event":"start","launch":"0371-demo-builder","n":10,"role":"demo-builder","msgs":["M-19","M-20","M-24"],"tasks":[],"cwd":"/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-two-corners-off-the-board","workdirs":["/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-two-corners-off-the-board","/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-pick-two-or-pick-four","/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-push-the-frame-over"],"tools":["Bash","Read","Write","Edit","Glob","Grep"],"sessionMin":60,"maxTurns":200,"settingSources":["project"]}
(node:270) [CLAUDE_SDK_CAN_USE_TOOL_SHADOWED] Warning: canUseTool will not be invoked for: Read, Glob, Grep. Bare allowedTools entries auto-approve the whole tool before the callback is consulted. To gate every tool call, use a PreToolUse hook; or remove the bare names from allowedTools so they fall through to canUseTool. Allow rules from settings files can also shadow the callback but are not visible here.
{"t":"2026-10-22T11:49:02.700Z","event":"finish","launch":"0122-demo-builder","n":4,"role":"demo-builder","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":141348,"cumulative":4538326,"cost":2.6989,"turns":50,"minutes":22.12,"sessions":["S-3"],"abandoned":[],"denials":1,"said":"I built both lessons and handed both in. Each passed the order's build check (`meta check`) before hand-in, and both went on to test1. The cap of 2 is reached and the session is closed.\n\n**1. O-1 · push-the-frame-over (parallelogram area): built, v1.**\n- **What it does:** a hinged 4 by 3 frame with five buttons: Lean to 60°, Lean to 30°, Cut and slide, Upright and Reset. The live readout shows sides, perimeter, height and area. The first cut while leaning leaves a mark on its button (\"✓ 4 × 1.50 = 6.0\"), so Reset can't wipe what the reveal quotes.\n- **Claims:** four, all `unverified`. One was added for the recall question.\n- **Stage text:** 15 words, within the 25 limit.\n- **Phone fit:** `reveal-fit` says it fits: nothing cropped at the top of the stage, and the reveal is 72 words.\n- **Departures from the brief:**\n  - The brief's stage size (320 × 200 px at 60 px per unit) can't hold the frame at 30°: it is about 6.6 units wide, which would be 396 px. I used 340 × 200 at 46 px per unit instead.\n  - \"Cut and slide\" is greyed out while the frame is upright, because there is nothing to cut and a button that changes nothing would fail QA.\n\n**2. O-3 · slice-a-corner-off (Euler's formula): built, v1.**\n- **What it does:** the solid is drawn as a wireframe with hidden edges dashed. Corners, edges and faces are counted from the drawn shape itself, not typed in. In the browser they matched the brief's numbers exactly: 8/12/6, 10/15/7, 12/18/8, 5/8/5 and 8/12/6. After each slice a line shows what changed, and both slices leave a mark on their buttons.\n- **Claims:** four, all `unverified`.\n- **Stage text:** 17 words, because I added the \"corners − edges + faces\" label the brief allowed.\n- **Phone fit:** fits, nothing cropped, reveal 77 words.\n- **Departure from the brief:** it calls the Euler claim's support a \"citation\", but the CLI only accepts derivation, simulation, source or convention, so I marked it `source`.\n\nThings that confused me:\n- **The build edits two unrelated files.** `next build` rewrites `tsconfig.json` and `src/data/editorial-profiles.account.json` in the worktree. I reverted both in each worktree before handing in.\n- **meta.json changed after hand-in.** push-the-frame-over's meta.json changed on disk after I handed it in, presumably from a code stage. I left it alone.\n- **Reset is never pressed on the QA path.** In push-the-frame-over, Upright and Reset both go back to the starting state, so after the QA path presses Upright, Reset is greyed out. Pre-flight question 6 (\"press Reset last\") therefore reads the reveal after Upright instead. The marks on the buttons still survive."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T11:49:43.579Z","event":"finish","launch":"0247-fact-checker","n":6,"role":"fact-checker","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":60518,"cumulative":535060,"cost":0.7977,"turns":18,"minutes":9.53,"sessions":["S-4"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I checked two lessons. The first goes back to build because its picture is wrong; the second passed. The session then closed because the queue was empty.\n\n**1. LESSON-push-the-frame-over (O-1): revise, sent back to build**\n- **Defect:** after \"Cut and slide\", the picture does not show a 4-wide rectangle, though the chip trace and the reveal both say it does. `Demo.tsx` fills only from x = c to x = 4 (`rect`), and c is the horizontal offset of the leaning side. At 30° that is 1.40 wide, so the screen shows a narrow rectangle and a separate triangle with a gap between them. The filled area comes to about 4.05, not 6.0. The fix is to fill from x = c to x = 4 + c.\n- **Claims:** c3 is marked disputed. Its wording is true, but the picture contradicts it. c1, c2 and c4 are verified: I re-derived the numbers and they match the brief's check script (G2).\n- **Record:** `company/reviews/push-the-frame-over/2026-10-22-fact-check.md`\n\n**2. LESSON-one-link-back-grows-the-core (O-10): pass, sent on to the learner review**\n- I recomputed the core from the lesson's own list of links. It has 4 pages at the start, 8 with I → F, 6 with J → G and 10 with both. That matches the claims, the readouts and the filled pages in the screenshots.\n- The cited textbook chapter is real. Its table of contents lists §13.3 \"The Web as a Directed Graph\" and §13.4 \"The Bow-Tie Structure of the Web\" ([Kleinberg's book page](https://cs.cornell.edu/home/kleinber/networks-book)).\n- All four claims are verified. One wording note doesn't block anything: c3's \"not every IN and OUT page\" really means \"not necessarily every\".\n- **Record:** `company/reviews/one-link-back-grows-the-core/2026-10-22-fact-check.md`\n\n**What confused me:** the role doc (`company/roles/fact-checker.md`) tells me to write to `progress.md`, my personal memory file and the board. Your brief says code owns those files, so I left all three alone. Nothing else got in the way."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T11:53:19.261Z","event":"finish","launch":"0302-learner-evaluator","n":7,"role":"learner-evaluator","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":72071,"cumulative":457246,"cost":0.5244,"turns":12,"minutes":6.03,"sessions":["S-5"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I reviewed one lesson and gave it **launch**; the order has moved on to the launch stage. After that the queue was empty and the CLI closed my session.\n\n**LESSON-one-link-back-grows-the-core (v1).** Review: `company/reviews/one-link-back-grows-the-core/2026-10-22-learner-knows-bow-tie.md`.\n- **What I checked:** I compared every arrow in the screenshots with the two loops the reveal names (F→E→A→B→C→H→I→F and J→G→B→C→D→J). The core sizes of 8, 6, 10 and 4 match the readout, the filled pages and the chip ticks.\n- **Why launch:** the prediction is a real surprise, because 10 is the tempting wrong answer. The reveal answers what a learner would be asking: why E, H and I join the core while G and J stay out.\n- **Notes that don't block launch:**\n  - There's no key saying a filled page means \"in the core.\"\n  - In the reveal screenshot, page G is drawn darker than J, though both are outside the core. It looks like a leftover highlight.\n  - \"One back link adds only the pages on the loop it closes\" is right for this example, where each link closes one loop. In a bigger graph a link can close several loops; the trust sheet words this more carefully.\n\n**What confused me:**\n- **No version stamp in the walkthrough.** The review needs `lesson version: v<N>`, but the walkthrough doesn't show it. After writing my findings I read only the `version` field (1) from `meta.json`, and the review says so.\n- **Two names for the verdict.** The review template treats \"pass\" as no verdict and requires \"launch\". The CLI only accepts `--verdict=pass|revise`. So the review file says `Verdict: launch` and I handed in with `--verdict=pass`, as my instructions said. The CLI accepted both."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T11:54:56.141Z","event":"finish","launch":"0358-head-of-product","n":9,"role":"head-of-product","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":83326,"cumulative":646594,"cost":0.6736,"turns":13,"minutes":6.2,"sessions":["S-7"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"**LESSON-one-link-back-grows-the-core (O-10), launch stage: go.** The order has moved on to the ship gates (`gates`). After that, the queue was empty and the session closed.\n\nI found no defects that block launch:\n- **Walkthrough:** the core counts it shows (4 / 8 / 6 / 10) match the brief's check.\n- **Prediction:** the question is a real choice, and the hollow G and J show the \"everything joins\" mistake to be wrong.\n- **Reveal:** it fits on a phone screen and keeps the disclosure that the 10-page web is a toy.\n- **Records:** all four claims are verified by the fact-checker, QA passed on phone and desktop, and the learner review is v1 with `Verdict: launch`.\n\nThe record is `company/rituals/records/2026-10-22-launch-review-one-link-back-grows-the-core.md`. It carries the three required objections (no analytics-steward predictions, accessibility advisory only, learning-designer merged into the builder) and four more:\n- **Reveal wording:** it says one back link adds \"only the pages on the loop it closes\". That is true on this stage, but in general one link can close several loops. A v2 could say \"loops\".\n- **Small visual issues:** G is drawn with a slightly heavier ring than J, no key says a filled node means \"in the core\", and None shows as active before any exploring.\n- **Bookkeeping:** `evidence.simulatedLearner` in meta.json is empty even though a learner review exists.\n- **Book reference:** the E&K section numbers are still marked unconfirmed.\n\n**One confusing point:** the walkthrough's trust sheet still says \"NOT YET CHECKED\" and \"0 browser QA runs\". That's because it was recorded before the fact-check stage ran, so I took claim status from meta.json instead."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T11:57:50.615Z","event":"start","launch":"0477-fact-checker","n":11,"role":"fact-checker","msgs":["M-37","M-38","M-39"],"tasks":[],"cwd":"/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-ant-on-a-cube","workdirs":["/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-ant-on-a-cube","/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-slice-a-corner-off","/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-friends-of-friends-overlap"],"tools":["Bash","Read","Write","Edit","Glob","Grep","WebFetch","WebSearch"],"sessionMin":30,"maxTurns":120,"settingSources":["project"]}
(node:270) [CLAUDE_SDK_CAN_USE_TOOL_SHADOWED] Warning: canUseTool will not be invoked for: Read, Glob, Grep, WebFetch, WebSearch. Bare allowedTools entries auto-approve the whole tool before the callback is consulted. To gate every tool call, use a PreToolUse hook; or remove the bare names from allowedTools so they fall through to canUseTool. Allow rules from settings files can also shadow the callback but are not visible here.
{"t":"2026-10-22T11:58:20.910Z","event":"finish","launch":"0136-demo-builder","n":5,"role":"demo-builder","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":173061,"cumulative":6637950,"cost":3.6853,"turns":60,"minutes":31.36,"sessions":["S-2"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I built both lessons in this session and handed both in. The session is now closed (it hit its cap of 2 items). Neither lesson has been through the official QA, walkthrough, fact-check or learner review yet; those are later stages.\n\n**1. LESSON-ant-on-a-cube (O-2), version 1: build stage passed.** The automated build check (test1) passed and the order has moved on.\n- **What the learner does:** a 1 m cube is drawn at an angle. Two buttons draw the routes you can see: along the edges (3.00 m) and a face diagonal then an edge (2.41 m). \"Unfold two faces\" swings one face open like a door into a flat 2 by 1 rectangle with a straight line of 2.24 m. \"Fold back up\" turns that line into the bent path crossing the shared edge at its midpoint. Each tried button keeps its length under its label, and the bent path stays faintly on the cube after Reset.\n- **On a 390×844 phone screen:** the whole reveal fits with the cube above it. The reveal is 82 words (limit 90) and the stage has 14 words (limit 25).\n- **Changes from the brief, written down for cm-math in build.md:**\n  - I unfolded the front and right faces, not the brief's top and front. The brief also asks for the net to fit 300 × 150 px, which only a sideways 2 by 1 rectangle does. Top and front would unfold into a tall rectangle and push the reveal off the phone screen. The maths is the same either way.\n  - The lesson starts with no route drawn, so the screen before the guess shows no length at all.\n  - I added two claims to the brief's three: one for the told sentence \"on a flat sheet a straight line is shortest\", and one for the recall question (a 2 m cube, about 4.5 m).\n\n**2. LESSON-new-friend-loosens-the-circle (O-5), version 1: handed in, waiting for test1.** The same check passed when I ran it before handing in.\n- **What the learner does:** Ana sits in the centre with friends B to E. Every pair of her friends is drawn, solid if they are friends and dashed if not, so \"3 of 6\" and \"of 10\" can be counted on the picture. The buttons \"Fay knows 1/2/3\" and \"No Fay\" give 0.4, 0.5, 0.6 and back to 0.5.\n- **On the phone screen:** it fits. The reveal is 87 words, close to the 90 limit. The stage has 17 words.\n- **Changes from the brief:**\n  - Claim 3 (the definition of clustering) is marked support \"source\", because the lesson format has no \"definition\" option.\n  - Claim 2 keeps the 0.3 case only because the recall question uses it; no button shows it.\n\n**Things that confused me:**\n- **No order ID for item 2:** the pack I got for the second item didn't show its order ID where I looked, so the check command failed with the lesson name. I found the ID (O-5) in the run's state file.\n- **A file changed while I worked on item 2:** the ant-on-a-cube meta.json changed on disk after I had handed it in. I assumed a later stage did it and left it alone.\n- **A 404 in the browser console:** every lesson page on the local server logs one for `/api/account/me`, including a published lesson I checked. The QA rules fail a lesson on console errors, so if the official QA run sees the same 404 it would flag it on every lesson, not just these two.\n\nThe details are in each lesson's `company/reviews/<slug>/build.md` and `design.md`."}
