{"t":"2026-10-22T12:03:50.202Z","event":"finish","launch":"0521-demo-builder","n":12,"role":"demo-builder","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":80320,"cumulative":1404083,"cost":0.8958,"turns":22,"minutes":4.44,"sessions":["S-11"],"abandoned":[],"denials":1,"said":"Both items were revises sent back by the fact-checker, and I've handed both in. My session hit its cap of 2 and is closed.\n\n**1. O-2, ant-on-a-cube (now v2), handed in and moving to test1.**\n- **Finding (c2):** \"unfolding two faces that share an edge\" puts the ant's corners at opposite ends only for one specific pair: a face at the start corner plus the adjacent face at the far corner. The reveal now says \"Unfolding the front and right faces…\", which are the two faces the stage actually unfolds, and c2 names that pair.\n- **Finding (c4):** the rule was worded for any surface. c4 now says \"on a box (a convex surface made of flat faces)\", and the reveal's last sentence says \"the best walk over a box is found by unfolding it\". I also narrowed `doesNotKnow` and design.md to boxes.\n- **Claims:** all five are back to `unverified` with no checkedBy/checkedOn.\n- **Records:** build.md has `## Pre-flight v2` and design.md has a revision note.\n- **Checks:** the order's test1 check passes. Typecheck is clean, and the production build succeeded. reveal-fit passed at 390×844 (fit 1, nothing cropped, phoneFit 1) with the reveal at about 84 words. I reverted the `tsconfig.json` rewrite the build makes.\n\n**2. O-3, slice-a-corner-off (now v2), handed in and moving to test1.**\n- **Finding (c2):** the rule \"a slice through a corner where k edges meet always adds k − 1 corners, k edges and 1 face\" is false when the slice reaches the neighbouring corners. Both c2 and the reveal now say \"a small slice that cuts only the k edges at a corner\".\n- **Claims:** all four are back to `unverified`.\n- **Records:** build.md has `## Pre-flight v2` and design.md has a revision note.\n- **Checks:** the order's test1 check passes. Only the wording changed and the reveal grew by two words (77 to about 79), so I did not rebuild or rerun reveal-fit; the qa stage will run them.\n\n**Confusing points:**\n- When I handed in the first item, `room next` gave me O-3 but its output was long, and the top of it (order, workdir and env) scrolled out of my tail. I read the workdir from `state.json`.\n- The guard (K10) refused one Bash heredoc that edited a file, although an earlier heredoc of the same kind went through. I made that edit with the Edit tool instead.\n- A hook blocks `pkill`, so I started and stopped the test server with `tools/serve.sh start|stop <port>`."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T12:06:20.583Z","event":"finish","launch":"0649-demo-builder","n":15,"role":"demo-builder","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":66864,"cumulative":629083,"cost":0.5176,"turns":10,"minutes":2.69,"sessions":["S-14"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I handed in one item, a revise of LESSON-friends-of-friends-overlap (order O-4). The lesson is now v2 and has moved on to test1. The queue was empty after that, so the session is over.\n\n**What I changed, in reply to the fact-check:**\n- **Source for claim c4:** I moved the citation from Easley & Kleinberg ch. 2 to ch. 20, The Small-World Phenomenon (Fig. 20.1). That chapter comes from the fact-checker's secondary search results; nobody has read the book itself because the proxy blocks both PDFs. So it is marked as needing a human source check, and the fact-checker can still only leave c4 unverified.\n- **Wording of c4:** it now says \"some friends of friends are already your friends, so the count two steps out is smaller\", instead of \"many … much smaller\".\n- **What the learner sees:** nothing changed. The reveal already limits the point to the village (\"In the village they do, so the count stays small\"), and claim c1 covers that, so I didn't touch Demo.tsx.\n- **Claim statuses:** all four claims are back to `unverified`, with the fact-checker's notes, checkedBy and checkedOn removed, as the revise rule requires for claims verified during this order. `meta.version` went from 1 to 2.\n- **Build note:** I added a \"Revise v2\" section and `## Pre-flight v2` to `company/reviews/friends-of-friends-overlap/build.md`.\n\n**Checks:** `meta check --order=O-4` passed (`ok = true`). `npm run check` fails with 811 errors, but none of them mention this lesson; the ones shown are in `company/decisions/` records. `tsconfig.json` and `AGENTS.md` were not touched.\n\n**Two things that confused me:**\n- `curriculum.references` in meta.json still points to ch. 2 (§2.3), because that reference comes from the brief, which cm-math owns. The stepping mechanic does fit ch. 2. Whether to add ch. 20 is cm-math's decision; I said so in the build note but did not raise a separate ask.\n- The kickoff text says to use `--cap=2`, but the pack said the queue held one item. That was correct: the session closed with \"queue empty\" after the first item."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T12:08:27.848Z","event":"finish","launch":"0580-learner-evaluator","n":13,"role":"learner-evaluator","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":73532,"cumulative":608576,"cost":0.5728,"turns":15,"minutes":5.98,"sessions":["S-12"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I reviewed one lesson, LESSON-new-friend-loosens-the-circle (v1), and gave it **launch**. The hand-in was accepted, the order moves on to the launch stage, and the session closed because the queue was empty.\n\n- **Review file:** `company/reviews/new-friend-loosens-the-circle/2026-10-22-learner-friend-pairs.md`, for a learner who can count friend pairs but has never met clustering.\n- **Why launch:** I counted every line in all five screenshots against the readout. In each state the picture, the readout, the ticks on the chips and the reveal all agree: 3 of 6, 4 of 10, 5 of 10, 6 of 10, then back to 3 of 6. The question defines clustering before using it, \"Higher\" is a tempting wrong answer, and the reveal explains why the number drops: Fay adds 4 pairs to the bottom but only one to the top for each friend she knows.\n- **Notes that don't block launch:**\n  - There is no key for the three line styles: grey lines are Ana's own friendships, solid coloured lines are linked pairs, dashed lines are unlinked pairs. A learner could count the grey lines by mistake, though the readout names what is counted.\n  - \"In your class\" in the question reads oddly.\n  - \"No Fay\" is highlighted before anything is pressed, which can briefly look like a preselected answer.\n\nOne thing confused me. The review template needs the lesson version, but `meta.json` was not on my reading list. I wrote my findings first, then read only the `version` field from `meta.json`, and said so in the review. I did not read `build.md` or `design.md`."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T12:09:12.147Z","event":"finish","launch":"0630-head-of-product","n":14,"role":"head-of-product","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":74221,"cumulative":464962,"cost":0.5402,"turns":9,"minutes":5.89,"sessions":["S-13"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I chaired the launch review for **LESSON-new-friend-loosens-the-circle** (v1). The decision is **go**, and the order has moved on to the ship gates (`gates` stage). The queue was empty after that, so the session closed after this one item.\n\n**Record:** `company/rituals/records/2026-10-22-launch-review-new-friend-loosens-the-circle.md`\n\n**Checks against the brief:** I read the walkthrough before the review records. It matches the brief:\n- The buttons are in the brief's order: \"Fay knows 1\", \"Fay knows 2\", \"Fay knows 3\", \"No Fay\".\n- I counted the lines on screen, and every readout is right: 4 of 10 = 0.4, 5 of 10 = 0.5, 6 of 10 = 0.6, and back to 3 of 6 with no Fay.\n- The closing explanation is about 75 words against a 90-word limit, fits on a phone screen, and quotes the values the learner saw.\n- The fact-checker verified all three claims, QA passed on phone and desktop, and the learner review says launch.\n\n**Objections recorded with the launch:**\n- **The three you required:** no analytics-steward predictions until M7; accessibility review is advisory and none was run; the learning-designer is merged into the builder.\n- **Claim c2 wording:** the \"Why trust this?\" sheet says Fay \"must know at least 2 of the 4 to keep it at 0.5\". It should say \"at least 0.5\", because knowing 3 gives 0.6. The fact-checker passed it and marked the fix optional, so I logged it for a v2.\n- **Learner review's minor notes:**\n  - The diagram has no key for its line styles.\n  - \"In your class\" reads oddly in the question.\n  - \"No Fay\" is highlighted before anything is pressed, so it looks pre-selected.\n- **Two bookkeeping gaps:**\n  - The walkthrough was recorded before the fact-check, so its \"Why trust this?\" sheet still shows NOT YET CHECKED.\n  - `evidence.simulatedLearner` in meta.json is empty even though a v1 learner review exists.\n\n**What confused me:** only the NOT YET CHECKED label, which conflicts with the verified claims in meta.json. I went by meta.json, as my notes from the previous order advised."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T12:11:03.580Z","event":"start","launch":"0802-fact-checker","n":16,"role":"fact-checker","msgs":["M-59","M-60","M-62","M-63","M-64"],"tasks":[],"cwd":"/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-not-every-circle-is-red","workdirs":["/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-not-every-circle-is-red","/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-ant-on-a-cube","/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-slice-a-corner-off","/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-friends-of-friends-overlap","/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-two-corners-off-the-board"],"tools":["Bash","Read","Write","Edit","Glob","Grep","WebFetch","WebSearch"],"sessionMin":30,"maxTurns":120,"settingSources":["project"]}
