{"t":"2026-10-22T13:45:14.868Z","event":"start","launch":"1487-head-of-product","n":26,"role":"head-of-product","msgs":["M-129"],"tasks":[],"cwd":"/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-friends-of-friends-overlap","workdirs":["/home/user/s3c-wt/base/.claude/worktrees/LESSON-friends-of-friends-overlap"],"tools":["Bash","Read","Write","Edit","Glob","Grep"],"sessionMin":30,"maxTurns":120,"settingSources":["project"]}
(node:270) [CLAUDE_SDK_CAN_USE_TOOL_SHADOWED] Warning: canUseTool will not be invoked for: Read, Glob, Grep. Bare allowedTools entries auto-approve the whole tool before the callback is consulted. To gate every tool call, use a PreToolUse hook; or remove the bare names from allowedTools so they fall through to canUseTool. Allow rules from settings files can also shadow the callback but are not visible here.
{"t":"2026-10-22T13:50:13.216Z","event":"finish","launch":"1444-fact-checker","n":24,"role":"fact-checker","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":64060,"cumulative":750997,"cost":0.8542,"turns":22,"minutes":7.57,"sessions":["S-30"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I checked two lessons this session and passed both. Each now goes on to the learner stage. The queue then ran empty and the session closed.\n\n**1. friends-of-friends-overlap (O-4, lesson v3): pass, all 4 claims verified.** Record: `company/reviews/friends-of-friends-overlap/2026-10-22-fact-check-v3.md`\n- **c1:** I re-ran the search over the 1,000-person ring myself. It gives 10 people at each of steps 1, 2 and 3, 31 within 3 steps counting you, and 100 for the farthest person.\n- **c2:** With no shared friends the counts are 90 at step 2, 810 at step 3 and 911 within 3.\n- **c3:** The ringed friend's 10 links are you, 6 of your own friends and 3 new people.\n- **c4:** The book citation is Easley & Kleinberg ch. 20, Fig. 20.1. The proxy blocked the chapter PDFs, so I confirmed it from search-result extracts of the Cornell ch. 20 PDF instead. That is weaker than reading the book. The section number is still unconfirmed.\n- I found no learner-visible fact without a claim.\n- The brief cites ch. 2, but the lesson cites ch. 20. Ch. 20 is the chapter that makes the argument, so the lesson is right and the brief should be updated to match.\n\n**2. push-the-frame-over (O-1, lesson v3): pass, all 4 claims verified.** Record: `company/reviews/push-the-frame-over/2026-10-22-fact-check-v3.md`\n- **c1:** I recomputed height and area at each angle: 3.00 and 12.0 upright, 2.60 and 10.4 at 60°, 1.50 and 6.0 at 30°.\n- **c2:** The perimeter stays 14 at every angle.\n- **c3:** The cut-and-slide does make a 4-wide rectangle of the same height. This holds because the top overhangs by at most 3, which is less than the base of 4, and the claim is limited to this frame. The drawn shapes use the same coordinates as the claim.\n- **c4:** The recall question's answer, 5 × 1 = 5, is correct.\n\n**What confused me:** both worktrees already had `-fact-check.md` and `-fact-check-v2.md` from earlier rounds. To keep my check independent I didn't open them, and wrote new `-v3.md` files, as my notes from earlier sessions advise.\n\nSources:\n- [E&K ch. 20, The Small-World Phenomenon (Cornell PDF)](https://www.cs.cornell.edu/home/kleinber/networks-book/networks-book-ch20.pdf)\n- [USP mirror of ch. 20](https://edisciplinas.usp.br/pluginfile.php/1148127/mod_resource/content/1/SmallWorlds.pdf)"}
{"t":"2026-10-22T13:51:02.038Z","event":"finish","launch":"1460-learner-evaluator","n":25,"role":"learner-evaluator","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":95599,"cumulative":833415,"cost":0.8704,"turns":22,"minutes":6.78,"sessions":["S-31"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I reviewed two lessons and gave both a launch verdict. Both orders have moved on to the launch stage. The queue then ran empty and the session closed.\n\n1. **O-4, friends-of-friends-overlap (v3): launch.** The 10/10/10 counts and the \"7 land on you or your own friends, only 3 are new\" line hold up: you can count the arcs from the ringed friend in the picture and get 5 + 2 = 7. The \"No shared friends\" column puts 90 and 810 beside the village's 10s. Non-blocking notes:\n   - \"within 3: 31\" includes you, but only the reveal says so.\n   - In the \"No shared friends\" picture, the \"you\" label overlaps a node.\n   \n   Review: `company/reviews/friends-of-friends-overlap/2026-10-22-learner-knows-multiplication-not-triangles.md`\n2. **O-1, push-the-frame-over (v3): launch.** The readout keeps sides and perimeter fixed while height and area fall (12.0, then 10.4, then 6.0). The cut-and-slide picture shows the 4 × 1.50 rectangle that the reveal describes. Non-blocking notes:\n   - The walkthrough path ends on \"Upright\", so the stage shows the upright frame when the reveal opens. The 1.50 and 6.0 are still on screen in the \"Cut and slide\" button's ✓ line, but the cut rectangle is not.\n   - The word \"parallelogram\" first appears in the reveal.\n   \n   Review: `company/reviews/push-the-frame-over/2026-10-22-learner-knows-rectangle-area.md`\n\n**What confused me:** the walkthrough doesn't give the lesson version, and I'm not allowed to read meta.json. I stamped both reviews v1, the leave check refused each one because meta.json is v3, and I re-stamped them v3. That cost one refused hand-in per lesson. Because these are v3, an earlier loop must have sent each order back. I assumed the walkthroughs were recorded for v3 but couldn't confirm that from what I'm allowed to read. It would help if the walkthrough transcript carried the version.\n\nOne small leftover: my sed edit left a lowercase/capital mismatch (\"; The leave check…\") in the first review's last line. It's cosmetic and doesn't affect the verdict."}
{"t":"2026-10-22T13:51:46.427Z","event":"finish","launch":"1487-head-of-product","n":26,"role":"head-of-product","ok":true,"reason":null,"tokens":102219,"cumulative":907472,"cost":0.9323,"turns":16,"minutes":6.53,"sessions":["S-32"],"abandoned":[],"denials":0,"said":"I chaired two launch reviews and gave both lessons **go**. Both are now at the ship gates. The session then ended because the queue was empty.\n\n**1. friends-of-friends-overlap (O-4, v3): go.** The record is `company/rituals/records/2026-10-22-launch-review-friends-of-friends-overlap.md`.\n- I recomputed the numbers on screen and they match: in the village, 10 people at each of steps 1–3 and 31 within 3 steps. With no shared friends, it's 90, 810 and 911.\n- The fact-checker verified all four claims, the QA run passed on phone and desktop, and the learner review says launch.\n- Objections carried in the record:\n  - The three standing ones: no analytics predictions, accessibility review is advisory and none was run, and the learning-designer is merged into the builder.\n  - Claim c4 (the citation to Easley & Kleinberg ch. 20) was verified from search snippets, because the proxy blocked the full text. Its source field still says it \"needs a human source check\", which reads oddly next to `verified`.\n  - The brief cites ch. 2 §2.3 while meta.json now cites ch. 20. cm-math should update the brief.\n  - Small learner-review notes, and the empty `evidence.simulatedLearner` in meta.json.\n\n**2. push-the-frame-over (O-1, v3): go.** The record is in the O-1 worktree (`.claude/worktrees/LESSON-push-the-frame-over`), at `company/rituals/records/2026-10-22-launch-review-push-the-frame-over.md`.\n- I recomputed: height 2.60 and area 10.4 at 60°, height 1.50 and area 6.0 at 30°, perimeter 14 throughout. The cut-and-slide works at every angle on this frame.\n- The earlier fact-check findings are fixed: the cut-state picture had the wrong width in v1, and c3 was stated too generally in v2. All four claims are verified, QA passed, and the learner review says launch.\n- Objections carried in the record:\n  - The same three standing ones.\n  - The reveal opens over the upright 12.0 frame while its text describes the 4 × 1.50 rectangle. The numbers are still on screen in the chip's record, but the rectangle itself is not.\n  - \"Parallelogram\" first appears in the reveal.\n  - Claim c4 on the trust sheet starts with the bare word \"Recall:\".\n  - `evidence.simulatedLearner` in meta.json is empty.\n\n**What confused me:**\n- The second item's files were in a different worktree from the workdir I was given at the start. I worked there because its pack named it.\n- Both walkthrough trust sheets still show \"NOT YET CHECKED\", because the walkthroughs were recorded before the fact-check. I judged claim status from meta.json instead."}
